1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,030
Pickup just moved earlier.

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:04,050
Your train is late. And dinner?

3
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:06,790
Still not sorted. Meet Relay Home.

4
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,070
One change, one evening to rethink.

5
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:10,610
Let's see how it works.

6
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:13,280
All the household data
in this demo is made up.

7
00:00:14,208 --> 00:00:18,858
First, Relay checks who's approved
to help, what everyone's schedule allows,

8
00:00:18,868 --> 00:00:20,598
and what's in the pantry.

9
00:00:20,608 --> 00:00:23,038
Jo can arrive fifteen minutes early.

10
00:00:23,048 --> 00:00:27,098
Dinner needs just three dollars
and twenty cents in extra ingredients.

11
00:00:27,108 --> 00:00:28,818
Those calls on screen?

12
00:00:28,828 --> 00:00:34,128
They're real MCP requests to our
self-hosted server over Streamable HTTP.

13
00:00:35,083 --> 00:00:36,913
But let's tighten the budget.

14
00:00:36,923 --> 00:00:39,233
Two dollars. Twenty minutes.

15
00:00:39,243 --> 00:00:44,153
Relay switches to chickpea tomato soup,
using what's already in the demo pantry.

16
00:00:44,163 --> 00:00:47,853
It's a deterministic planner,
not a general language model.

17
00:00:47,863 --> 00:00:52,883
The same MCP tools also accept
structured requests from another client.

18
00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:55,820
Looks good? You confirm.

19
00:00:55,830 --> 00:00:58,580
Relay saves the local
tasks and shopping list.

20
00:00:58,590 --> 00:01:01,200
It hasn't messaged Jo or bought anything.

21
00:01:01,210 --> 00:01:03,960
Pickup still needs a real acknowledgment.

22
00:01:03,970 --> 00:01:06,780
Stale previews, expired
plans, and repeat clicks

23
00:01:06,790 --> 00:01:10,990
can't silently turn
into extra commitments.

24
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,530
Now refresh.

25
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:14,050
The plan is still here.

26
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:15,890
So is the conversation.

27
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:18,090
And this isn't just browser memory.

28
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:22,860
Our integration tests restart the server
and check that the same state comes back.

29
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:26,097
Changed your mind? Undo.

30
00:01:26,107 --> 00:01:29,517
Previous tasks, preferences,
and the shopping list come back.

31
00:01:29,527 --> 00:01:31,157
The change is recorded.

32
00:01:31,167 --> 00:01:34,007
And the assistant can't
press confirm for you.

33
00:01:34,667 --> 00:01:36,657
Now Jo can't make it.

34
00:01:36,667 --> 00:01:38,837
Nobody approved can arrive on time.

35
00:01:38,847 --> 00:01:41,977
Relay says so, and removes
the confirm action.

36
00:01:41,987 --> 00:01:45,757
No guessing. No handing pickup
to an unapproved neighbor.

37
00:01:45,767 --> 00:01:48,887
An honest blocker beats
a reassuring mistake.

38
00:01:49,417 --> 00:01:52,407
Good news: Sam's meeting ends early.

39
00:01:52,417 --> 00:01:54,467
That makes the old preview stale.

40
00:01:54,477 --> 00:01:57,407
Replan, and now a parent can make pickup.

41
00:01:57,417 --> 00:02:02,467
This is an independent Alexa-plus
simulation, not a live Alexa connection.

42
00:02:02,477 --> 00:02:07,357
The app runs locally, with no
paid API or device required.

43
00:02:08,125 --> 00:02:10,935
But what if Sam declines
after you've saved?

44
00:02:10,945 --> 00:02:12,575
Record that response.

45
00:02:12,585 --> 00:02:16,675
Relay restores the previous local plan,
excludes Sam, and checks the other

46
00:02:16,685 --> 00:02:19,335
approved helpers through MCP.

47
00:02:19,345 --> 00:02:21,535
Jo becomes a new proposal.

48
00:02:21,545 --> 00:02:23,235
Still no message sent.

49
00:02:23,245 --> 00:02:24,565
Still your decision.

50
00:02:25,333 --> 00:02:27,003
One more refresh.

51
00:02:27,013 --> 00:02:28,503
What does Relay remember?

52
00:02:28,513 --> 00:02:31,423
Jo is a draft, not a confirmed pickup.

53
00:02:31,433 --> 00:02:34,003
Earlier saved changes are kept distinct.

54
00:02:34,013 --> 00:02:38,663
Another MCP client can read that
context after a server restart.

55
00:02:38,673 --> 00:02:41,223
Twenty-four automated tests pass.

56
00:02:41,233 --> 00:02:44,458
Plans change. You stay in control.
